WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.705
You know your subject.

00:00:01.705 --> 00:00:06.822
How do you turn it into a course people can actually
follow?

00:00:06.822 --> 00:00:08.953
Welcome to Elevate for Humanity.

00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:11.512
I am PARIS, your AI presenter.

00:00:11.512 --> 00:00:17.480
The store describes a course creation workspace with AI
assisted blueprints, lessons, assessments, narration,

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.760
and learner delivery.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.597
Start with an outcome, not a pile of slides.

00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:28.566
For a business orientation, the outcome might be that a
participant can find their

00:00:28.566 --> 00:00:32.829
dashboard, understand the schedule, and identify the
right support contact.

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:35.387
Break that outcome into short lessons.

00:00:35.387 --> 00:00:40.504
Add an example, a practice task, and a useful check for
understanding.

00:00:40.504 --> 00:00:45.620
Review AI generated material for accuracy,
accessibility, and fit for your learners.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.883
Have a qualified instructor review technical content and
assessment answers.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:54.573
Use your own materials or content you have permission to
use.

00:00:54.573 --> 00:01:00.542
A course completion certificate is different from a
professional license or an external certification.

00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:06.511
The plan page lists monthly generation credits, so plan
media production around the applicable

00:01:06.511 --> 00:01:06.937
allowance.

00:01:06.937 --> 00:01:12.906
A useful first project is a three lesson orientation:
welcome and navigation, responsibilities and

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.464
schedule, then support and next steps.

00:01:15.464 --> 00:01:18.449
Test it as a learner before publishing.

00:01:18.449 --> 00:01:24.418
Explore the course builder through Elevate's store, and
follow this show for examples of

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:26.976
clearer teaching and lighter administrative work.

